<https://example.org/slice/unit:sha256:a2c89617788d82fe98fd7638e95046fcacfb540b68dd2c74a9f2ce670b4eb4f2> <https://example.org/slice/text> "3. Between the Anvil and the Comb the shelf drops away in three steps,\nand each step keeps its own crowd: the first holds the banded urchins\nthat the fishers call pinheads, the second the pale fans 🐚 that close\nat a shadow and open again a slow count later, and the third nothing at\nall that a diver has yet named, only a cold green water that the light\ngives up on well before the floor of it is reached by any lamp we own." .
